<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n50731" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Vestīni</span></b> , ōrum,
			m., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a people of Central Italy</i>, <i>on the Adriatic
				Sea</i>, <i><span class="en">Auct. Her. 2, 28, 45</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">Liv. 8,
				29</span></i>; <i><span class="en">10, 3</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">Plin.
				3, 12, 17, § 107</span></i>.— Hence, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Vestīnus</span></b> , a,
			um, adj., <i>of</i> or <i>belonging to the Vestini</i>: Vestina virum vis,
			Enn. ap. <i><span class="en">Charis. p. 251</span></i> P. (Ann. v.
			280 Vahl.); so, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">populus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv. 8,
					29</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cohors,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					44, 40</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">juventus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sil.
					8, 516</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">senex,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Juv.
					14, 181</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">aquae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Luc.
					2, 425</span></i>
			.</div>
